further:
  - slug: mari-syria
    why: Mari and Eshnunna were at war between the 3rd and the 5th (2nd and 4th)
      years of Zimri-Lim, and most of what is known about Eshnunna's diplomacy
      comes from letters in the Mari archives.
  - slug: babylon
    why: In 1762 BC, in Year 31 of Hammurabi of Babylon, the Babylonians occupied
      Eshnunna; in his 38th year name Hammurabi claimed to have destroyed it
      with a flood.
  - slug: assur
    why: An army of Eshnunna took Assur and Ekallatum, and a letter to Zimri-Lim
      reported that "Assur, Ekallatum and Eshnunna have now become one house."
